<title>COSTA RICA: Costa Rica says to issue $200 million bonds.</title>
<headline>Costa Rica says to issue $200 million bonds.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Costa Rica 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Costa Rica will issue $200 million worth of bonds in September, the government said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;In September, we will place on sale the first $200 million that will help us solve our serious internal debt problem,&quot; Minister of Information Alejandro Soto said at a news conference.</p>
<p>The issue will form part of the $500 million that Costa Rica plans to put on sale in international markets to help it cut its outstanding debt.</p>
</text>
